# The negation of a BallVector with 2-limb centers (milestone2.md, "BallVector": bv_neg_k): each center
# negated limb by limb (neg_2), the radius unchanged (bv_neg_radius): exact, the result is exactly the
# set of the negated members. The state is that of norm_upper_2 on the centers written, and the finish
# norm_finish_1: the operand that is the whole space gives the whole space.
fold:          bv_neg_2
arrays:        stored x = x0 x1
scalars:       stored rx
state:         m, mask ok
step:          z = neg_2(x)
record:        (m, ok) = norm_step_2(m, ok, z)
combine:       (m, ok) = norm_combine(m, ok, m, ok)
radius:        rz = bv_neg_radius(m, rx)
finish:        (r, finite) = norm_finish_1(rz, ok)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z = z0 z1
output:        r
output:        mask finite
value:         -x
requires:      ball_vector x rx
ensures:       encloses_entries z r -x x=x,rx flag=finite finite_when=abs_le(abs(x)+rx,1) radii_when=abs_le(rx,1) exact
min_precision: 1
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
source:        neg_2 on each center, the radius of ball_neg_2 (milestone2.md, BallVector)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
